<title>USA: General Dynamics shrs rally on Lockheed deal.</title>
<headline>General Dynamics shrs rally on Lockheed deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stock investors backed General Dynamics Corp's intented acquisition of Lockheed Martin Corp's armament and defense systems units, pushing the shares 2-3/8 higher to 69-5/8 in Thursday morning NYSE trade.</p>
<p>Lockheed, meanwhile, slipped 3/9 to 90.</p>
<p>General Dynamics announced early Thursday the $450 million deal, which has been approved by the boards of both companies and remains subject to regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>The units together are expected to produce $500 million in 1996 revenue.</p>
</text>
